.Dd August 7, 2026
.Dt JEEP-UNINSTALL 1
.Os Jeep DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm jeep-uninstall
.Nd uninstall a bundle
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo
.Ar bundle
.No ...
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
uninstalls a bundle.
For Janet bundles,
the bundle is uninstalled using the
.Ql "bundle/uninstall"
function.
For JPM bundles,
.Nm
will use the JPM bundle manifest and remove the paths specified
in that file.
.Pp
If
.Ar bundle
is omitted,
.Nm
will try to uninstall a bundle based on information in the current
working directory.
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Ar bundle
.No ...
.Xc
One or more bundles to uninstall.
Each value must be the name of an installed bundle.
.El
.Pp
For more information about
.Sy JPM bundles
and
.Sy Janet bundles ,
see CONCEPTS in
.Xr jeep 1 .
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To uninstall two bundles,
.Ql "foo"
and
.Ql "bar" :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep uninstall foo bar
.Ed
.
